          %hr/
          %h2#20090731 2009-07-31
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
                fixed a mistake at
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+foundation"} axiom of foundation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"}> Ronnie Brown
                \: Added in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+cubical+sets"} connection on cubical sets
                a reference to a recent preprint of Maltsiniotis showing that cubical sets with connections form a
                = succeed "," do
                  %em strict test category in the sense of Grothendieck
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran Škoda
                \: added a version (in my understanding) of main definitions in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+scheme"} almost scheme
                and made a longer heuristical quote from Gabber-Romero Introduction chapter. Created stub
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat%C3%A9gories+Tannakiennes"} Catégories Tannakiennes
                about the Deligne’s seminal paper and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Des+cat%C3%A9gories+ab%C3%A9liennes"} Des catégories abéliennes
                about Pierre Gabriel’s thesis.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    wrote a long “Idea” section at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
                    and polished/expanded the rest, following comments by
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                %li
                  %p
                    added to the “Idea” section at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                    a paragraph that gives some categorical or otherwise abstract nonsense description of how to make precise the statement that “a differential form is something that may be integrated”.
                %li
                  %p
                    created an entry
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Models+for+Smooth+Infinitesimal+Analysis"} Models for Smooth Infinitesimal Analysis
                    (so far containing just a summary and an incomplete link list) and linked to it from
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connection"} Ehresmann connection
                  %p
                    I am thinking that section IV there,
                    %em Cohomology and Integration
                    would be a good candidate for the high-brow abstract nonsense aspect section to be written at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                %li
                  %p
                    added expositional text to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
                    prodded by the blog discussion
                    %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/12/groupoidification_from_sigmamo.html#c025677"} here
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"}> Toby Bartels
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Created
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
                %li
                  Additions to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular space
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separation axiom
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
          %h2#20090730 2009-07-30
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    edited the intro to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
                    a bit more
                %li
                  %p
                    added to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
                    the Weibel reference
                %li
                  %p
                    linked to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
                    from
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
                %li
                  %p
                    added to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
                    an example section with the examples needed at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
                %li
                  %p
                    added various things to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"}> Toby Bartels
                \: More discussion at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categorical+hom-space"} (infinity,1)-categorical hom-space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran Škoda
                \: It looks correctly to me (I do not recall what wording I wrote and it looks like reading my mind). Bt it is late night and I should reread the whle entry rested at the day time. I created a stub version of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schematic+algebras"} schematic algebras
                (with references) and linked it at
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+schemes"} almost schemes
                (just created unfinished entry) in commutative geometry, but the reflective localizations are used to define ‘exotic’ affines to start with. Gabber-Lorenzo’s book is an egregious sample of how a modern algebraic geometer of Grothendieck’s school develops the theory of schemes and in a way it is a build ground-up with requiring sofistication level, but not many concrete details from the usual theory of schemes.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"}> Toby Bartels
                \: Please check that I rephrased the definition correctly at
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+scheme"} noncommutative scheme
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    replied at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categorical+hom-space"} (infinity,1)-categorical hom-space
                %li
                  %p
                    have to think about the question at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
                    (which in any case shows that I phrased the sentence too carelessly)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran Škoda
                \: created first draft of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+scheme"} noncommutative scheme
                (after Rosenberg), and plan in few minutes to start
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schematic+algebra"} schematic algebra
                (after van Oystaeyen). Somebody should also add
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+projective+geometry"} noncommutative projective geometry
                (after Artin and Zhang). It is a pity that only few of the most stubborn contributors use summer to add new material…
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                added some clauses to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
                and have some comments in a query box: I am thinking what the entry tries to define should be discussed at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
                while “Grothendieck group” should be the definition of a group structure on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi A
