                    = succeed "-action" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %p
                    But the point is that Jardine works in the “petit topos” perspective where all bundles live over the fixed site. So the terminal object in his setup is not the point, but the underlying space over which one works. This means that the simple picture of a principal
                    = succeed "-bundle" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %p
                    On the other hand, when one works with simplicial sheaves in the context of a “gros topos” such as sheaves on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Diff
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
                    or on open subsets of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                    or equivalent, then the simple conceptual picture remains valid.
                  %p
                    Notice that placing oneself into the context of
                    = succeed "-groupoids" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Diff
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
                  %p Evidently i shouldn’t be discussing this here but in some entry. But it’s time for me to go to bed now.
